From: Mahdi Taziki <61482609+Mhd-tz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Search the D3DMetal toolkit's DLL folder first when requested.

The DLLs of Apple's Game Porting Toolkit (d3d12, d3d12core, dxgi, d3d11, d3d10, …) are marked as Wine builtins. Wine
loads a builtin from its search path in order, and its own library folder comes first, so the runtime's d3d12.dll and
DXMT's dxgi.dll would always win over the toolkit's. WINE_D3DMETAL_DLLPATH (an absolute path, e.g.
<toolkit>/redist/lib/wine) is put before the runtime's folder; that folder's x86_64-unix/*.so are the toolkit's links
to libd3dshared.dylib, found by Wine's normal lookup. Unset, empty or relative: the search path is exactly as before.

AnvilMac sets it only for a game whose setup is D3DMetal, only to its own verified copy of the toolkit, and never
while preparing a prefix (wineboot would copy the toolkit's DLLs into system32).

Provenance (recorded by AnvilMac, 2026-10-18): written for AnvilMac, not from CrossOver (its source has the same
search order). Copyright 2026 Mahdi Taziki. License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (Wine).
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -295,13 +295,16 @@
 static void set_dll_path(void)
 {
     char *p, *path = getenv( "WINEDLLPATH" );
+    /* D3DMetal bridge: the user's toolkit DLLs before the runtime's own (AnvilMac, 2026-10-18; see patch header) */
+    const char *d3dmetal_path = getenv( "WINE_D3DMETAL_DLLPATH" );
     int i, count = 0;
 
     if (path) for (p = path, count = 1; *p; p++) if (*p == ':') count++;
 
-    dll_paths = malloc( (count + 2) * sizeof(*dll_paths) );
+    dll_paths = malloc( (count + 3) * sizeof(*dll_paths) );
     count = 0;
 
+    if (d3dmetal_path && d3dmetal_path[0] == '/') dll_paths[count++] = strdup( d3dmetal_path );
     if (!build_dir) dll_paths[count++] = dll_dir;
 
     if (path)
